Each faucet contributes equally, so one faucet's rate is:

\[
\text{Rate of one faucet} = \frac{50}{3} \div 3 = \frac{50}{9} \text{ gallons per minute}
\]

With six faucets, the total rate is:

\[
6 \times \frac{50}{9} = \frac{300}{9} = \frac{100}{3} \text{ gallons per minute}
\]

To fill a 25-gallon tub at this rate, the time required is:

\[
\text{Time} = \frac{25}{\frac{100}{3}} = \frac{75}{100} = 0.75 \text{ minutes} = 45 \text{ seconds}
\]

