To solve the system of equations for the ordered pair of integers \((x, y)\):

\[
\begin{cases}
12x + 21y = 15 \\
21x + 12y = 51
\end{cases}
\]

\textbf{Step 1: Simplify the Equations}

Divide both equations by 3 to simplify:

\[
\begin{cases}
4x + 7y = 5 \\
7x + 4y = 17
\end{cases}
\]

\textbf{Step 2: Use the Elimination Method}

Multiply the first equation by 7 and the second by 4:

\[
\begin{cases}
28x + 49y = 35 \\
28x + 16y = 68
\end{cases}
\]

Subtract the second equation from the first:

\[
33y = -33 \implies y = -1
\]

\textbf{Step 3: Substitute \(y\) Back into One of the Equations}

Substitute \(y = -1\) into \(4x + 7y = 5\):

\[
4x - 7 = 5 \implies 4x = 12 \implies x = 3
\]

\textbf{Answer:}

\[
\boxed{(3,\, -1)}
\]

